<div class="page">
  <div class="section-heading">Section 4 - First Aid Measures</div>
  <div class="subsection-heading">01135 HEXANES</div>

  <div class="subsection-heading">First Aid:</div>
  <p>INHALATION: REMOVE TO FRESH AIR. TREAT SYMPTOMATICALLY. SKIN/EYES: IMMEDIATELY FLUSH W/PLENTY OF WATER FOR 15 MINS. INGESTION: DON'T INDUCE VOMITING. OBTAIN MEDICAL ATTENTION IN ALL CASES.</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-heading">Section 5 - Fire Fighting Measures</div>
  <div class="subsection-heading">01135 HEXANES</div>

  <div class="subsection-heading">Fire Fighting Procedures:</div>
  <p>WEAR SCBA & PROTECTIVE CLOTHING. USE WATER W/CAUTION. MATERIAL IS LIGHTER THAN WATER & INSOLUBLE IN WATER. THE FIRE COULD EASILY SPREAD BY THE USE OF WATER IN AN AREA WHERE THE WATER COULD NOT BE CONTAINED. WATER MAY BE INEFFECTIVE IN FIGHTING FIRE. USE WATER SPRAY TO KEEP FIRE-EXPOSED CONTAINERS COOL.</p>

  <div class="subsection-heading">Unusual Fire or Explosion Hazard:</div>
  <p>VAPORS ARE HEAVIER THAN AIR & MAY TRAVEL ALONG THE GROUND/BE MOVED BY VENTILATION TO AN IGNITION SOURCE & FLASH BACK. VAPORS MAY IGNITE EXPLOSIVELY. PREVENT BUILDUP OF VAPORS TO EXPLOSIVE CONCENTRATIONS.</p>

  <div class="subsection-heading">Extinguishing Media:</div>
  <p>WATER SPRAY, DRY CHEMICAL, CO2, FOAM</p>

